The attached image, Figure 6 from the npj Vaccines paper, illustrates how Nano-11 improves antigen targeting to immunopotentiating cells and increases antigen retention. Panel A shows that migratory dendritic cells (MigDCs) exhibit the highest expression of the costimulatory molecule CD86, indicating their strong immunopotentiating capacity for T cell activation. Panel B further characterizes OVA-positive MigDCs by CD11b and Ly6C markers, showing that ovalbumin (OVA) is largely contained within CD11b+ dendritic cells when adjuvanted with Nano-11. Panel C, a series of whole-mouse fluorescent images, demonstrates that Nano-11, similar to aluminum hydroxide (AH), significantly prolongs the retention of Alexa Fluor 647-labeled ovalbumin at the intramuscular injection site over seven days compared to soluble ovalbumin, which clears rapidly.